+### Target folder and consumers
+
+[ADR-0023](../adr/0023-os-targets.md) defines the target layout;
+[policy-gate/v1](../specs/policy-gate/v1.md) keeps the procedure shared and its
+OS-specific inputs target-owned. `ubuntu-26.04` is the first and currently only target;
+bash remains the only accepted shell.
+
+- **REPL start-up (built)** reads `target.toml`, selecting by os-release `ID` and `VERSION_ID`
+  exactly, with no `ID_LIKE` or nearby-version fallback. No match requires an explicit
+  `--target <id>` or `target =` in config. A named mismatch currently prints a warning.
+  Command prompts load from the target's `prompts/`.
+- **REPL inputs (planned)** include `model.toml` for weight hash validation and
+  `sensitive.toml` for sensitive locations/environment dumpers; these consumers are not built.
+- **Gate integration (planned, #12, #190)** is not built: the gate must use the target's
+  package-owner query from `target.toml`, `sensitive.toml` and `allowlist.toml`.
+  A mismatched named target must require confirmation for every command; this is planned,
+  not enforced by the current start-up warning. Gate-vector loading from
+  `gate-vectors.toml` already exists for gate tests; it is not REPL gate integration.
+- **Reader module (built, not yet wired into the REPL)** loads `prompts/reader.yaml`
+  and uses the target's `[command_provider]` configuration for package-provider lookup.
+- **Installer and packaging (planned, #48, #50)** must ship every target's runtime data
+  and use `model.toml` to download and verify weights. Targets are not packaged yet.
+- **Pipeline (planned)** reads `prompts/`, `harvest.toml` (harvest recipe and VM image),
+  and `eval/` (frozen split and target probes). Neither `harvest.toml` nor `eval/` exists yet.
+
+The current folder contains only `target.toml`, `sensitive.toml`, `gate-vectors.toml`
+and `prompts/`. `model.toml`, `allowlist.toml`, `harvest.toml` and `eval/` are planned.
+Model integrity and adapter compatibility remain requirements awaiting implementation.
+Runtime data is intended to ship; harvest/eval material is build-time only, and weights
+are referenced rather than stored in the folder (section 7).
